    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Driver D-10671 filed this dispute. The fare ledger (EV-FARE-06058) records the 5.00 SGD no-show fee charged at 09:09:34 and then returned to rider R-80737 and withheld from the driver at 09:29:30 as an interim reversal after the rider's complaint. Because the driver is the filing party, the question is whether that 5.00 SGD should be restored to him, and on this record it should.\n\nThe no-show was valid. The pickup was scheduled for 09:00 and the driver arrived at 09:02:40. Under POL-NS-21, because he arrived after the scheduled time, the 300-second free wait ran from his arrival and expired at 09:07:40; he cancelled at 09:09:30, 110 seconds later — exactly what POL-NS-21 permits. The arrival is GPS-corroborated (EV-GPS-06058: nearest fix 6.48 m from the pickup, inside the 50 m STANDARD radius, reported at 5 m accuracy inside the 25 m filter).\n\nThe rider's grounds for refusing to pay do not hold. POL-NS-24 (driver no-show) is not engaged: the deadline was 09:05:00 and the driver arrived at 09:02:40, so the rider may not cancel at no charge and no full refund is due. The driver's lateness is real and he concedes it in his own 09:03:00 message ('Hi, sorry a bit late'), but POL-NS-21 expressly contemplates a scheduled trip where the driver arrives after the scheduled time and starts the free wait from arrival; arriving after 09:00 was therefore a lateness the policy absorbs, and the rider's 'the driver was late, so I should not pay anything' is answered by the schedule she was given and the time he actually arrived, not by her history (POL-GEN-01). POL-NS-23 (contact obligation) is satisfied, not breached: two in-app messages (09:03:00 and 09:06:20) and a placed in-app call (09:05:10), all before the 09:09:30 cancellation, with both messages read by the rider.\n\nThe rider's alternative ask for a human reviewer is refused. No clause makes the rider's physical presence a fact the charge must establish, and nothing requires the trace to carry a rider track; the no-show determination rests on the expired free wait and the cancellation, both established on the record. The one missing artifact, the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-06058-01 (status MISSING, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT), carries no fact and no rule needs it, so POL-GEN-26 raises no open question here.\n\nUnder POL-NS-22 the fee therefore stands, and because the money has already moved the ruling restores it to the driver: DRIVER_COMPENSATION, with amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both 5.00. The fee charged is exactly the 5.00 SGD policy fee, so no POL-NS-22 fee-amount referral arises, and the driver met the deadline and the contact obligation, so no POL-NS-24 goodwill credit arises. The rider's no_show_cancellations_30d of 4 triggers the POL-NS-25 account review set out in the referrals. Confidence is 0.9, capped by the 1.0 weight_multiplier shared by the trip record, GPS trace, chat log and fare ledger that carry the deciding facts; at 5.00 SGD the dispute is below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, neither profile carries a fraud flag, and POL-NS-26 makes the AI ruling final."
  },
