    "explanation": "Both submissions have been weighed against the NO_SHOW_CHARGE policy. To the driver: your claim succeeds. The record shows you arrived at the pickup at 09:02:40 — after the 09:00 scheduled pickup — so under POL-NS-21 the 300-second free wait ran from your arrival and expired at 09:07:40; you cancelled at 09:09:30, 110 seconds after it expired, so the no-show condition is met. Your arrival is GPS-corroborated to the category's arrival test (EV-GPS-06058: nearest fix 6.48 m from the pickup, accuracy 5 m, inside the 50 m STANDARD radius and the 25 m filter), you met the POL-NS-23 contact obligation (two in-app messages at 09:03:00 and 09:06:20, and an in-app call at 09:05:10, all before the cancellation), and the 5.00 SGD charged matches the 5.00 SGD policy fee (POL-NS-22). Because that 5.00 SGD was reversed to the rider and recovered from you at 09:29:30 as an interim measure, the ruling moves the same 5.00 SGD back to you: DRIVER_COMPENSATION, with amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both 5.00. To the rider: your objections do not defeat the fee. The lateness the driver admits does not engage POL-NS-24, which voids the fee only if the driver arrives after the scheduled time plus 5 minutes (09:05:00); he arrived at 09:02:40, before that deadline (arrived_by_deadline = true), and he attempted contact, so neither a FULL_REFUND nor the POL-NS-24 5.00 SGD goodwill credit arises, and the missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-06058-01, MISSING, weight 0.0) carries no fact and justifies nothing. Nor does the absence of any observation of you create the open question POL-GEN-26 needs: the policy's test for the fee is the free wait plus a cancellation after it (POL-NS-21, POL-NS-22), not independent observation of the rider. Your profile fields (rating, account age, lifetime trips and the rest) are context only under POL-GEN-01 and decide nothing. Confidence: the contested value is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, so the AI ruling is final at any confidence and POL-NS-26 makes it final; neither profile carries a fraud flag, and the deciding facts rest on complete weight-1.0 artifacts (trip record and GPS trace for arrival and timing, chat log for contact, fare ledger for the 5.00 SGD fee). A clause-mandated referral follows: POL-NS-25, the rider's repeat no-show flag."
